200 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 199 0 R
  /Alt (Four-panel diagram showing neural integration mechanisms for multimodal fusion. Top-left panel labeled Early Fusion shows three inputs G (Gaze), S (Speech), U (UI) concatenated then passed through a joint encoder to produce output h. Top-right panel labeled Late Integration shows each modality with its own encoder (f_g, f_s, f_u), outputs combined through a fusion layer with sigmoid activation to produce y. Bottom-left panel labeled Cross-Modal Attention shows Gaze input generating Query Q, while Speech and UI generate Key K and Value V, with attention mechanism producing gaze-conditioned output h_g. Bottom-right panel labeled Gated Multimodal Units shows Gaze passing through tanh activation, Speech and UI through encoder h_su, with a learnable gate z controlling the weighted combination producing final output h. Legend indicates G equals Gaze in orange, S equals Speech in blue, U equals UI in gray, and Output in green.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
    /BBox [413.28085 87.242584 801.8898 364.8204]
  >>]
