306 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 33 0 R
  /Alt (Architectural diagram of a standards-oriented multimodal pipeline integrating gaze, voice, and DOM inputs. The pipeline flows left to right through five stages: (1) Acquisition via Web APIs including a proposed permission-gated Gaze Tracking API, Media Capture and WebRTC for audio streams with timestamps, and DOM and Accessibility Tree for element IDs and bounding boxes; (2) Normalization and Privacy with on-device processing boundary, privacy filter ensuring no raw video retention and coarse gaze vectors, producing normalized GazeEvent and SpeechEvent schemas; (3) Temporal Alignment using a shared timeline with monotonic timestamps and jitter compensation, plus a context window of plus or minus 500ms around speech to capture gaze lead; (4) Fusion and Interpretation through a multimodal encoder processing gaze, speech, and UI tokens, task heads for deictic resolution, turn-taking prediction, and barge-in detection, with policy constraints for consent state, accessibility fallback, and confidence thresholds; (5) Agent Outputs producing GroundingEvent, TurnEvent, and BargeInEvent that drive agent actions including element highlighting, spoken responses, and floor management.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
    /BBox [1.9055119 58.767212 839.98425 384.79578]
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 430 0 R
>>
endobj

