  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 309 0 R
  /Alt (Diagram illustrating gaze-grounded reference resolution on a web dashboard. A user views dashboard.example.com containing a sidebar with Overview, Metrics, and Settings navigation, plus three panels: Panel A (Chart), Panel B (Metric), and Panel C (Table). The user asks 'What does this mean?' while gaze tracking shows fixation at pixel coordinates (812, 182) for 420ms. A DOM Match box displays the resolution process: 3 candidate elements within the region of interest, panel B selected with 0.86 confidence, and approximately 300ms gaze lead time. The system highlights Panel B with a dashed orange border and provides an explanation of the highlighted element.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
